Improved detection of CTFE-only template instances

Template instances that are only used at compile time, such as in an `enum` initializer, UDA, or static if condition, used to be
emitted into the object file.
Only an eponymous `enum` template with a value of a basic type or `string` was skipped.
Now every template instance that is only used at compile time is skipped:

---
struct S { int a, b; }

// Already skipped before
template fieldCount(T)
{
    size_t count() { return T.tupleof.length; }
    enum fieldCount = count();
}
static assert(fieldCount!S == 2);

// Also skipped now
string repeat(string s)(size_t n)
{
    string r;
    foreach (i; 0 .. n)
        r ~= s;
    return r;
}
enum line = repeat!"-"(40);

struct Point(T)
{
    T x, y;
    T sum() const { return x + y; }
}
enum total = Point!int(1, 2).sum();
---

Previously, `repeat!"-"`, `Point!int.sum` and the druntime array-appending internals
used by `repeat` were emitted, even though nothing calls them at run time.

This makes object files and libraries smaller.
At time of writing, this reduces Phobos's size from 9091 members (19.7 MB) to 8230 (18.3 MB).
